{
  "title": "Split scraping/mod.rs and steps.rs; stop swallowing mark_failed \
errors in run_photo_import_job",
  "description": "Two structural problems plus one correctness wart in the \
scraping module:\n\
\n\
1. server/src/scraping/mod.rs (1204 lines) bundles unrelated responsibilities: \
host-allowlist parsing (74-134), step-registry construction (157), 7 \
job-creation constructors (231-419), job spawning, photo-import orchestration \
(458-570), job status CRUD helpers (591-718), pipeline execution (780-1054), \
and retry logic (1055). Split into scraping/allowlist.rs, scraping/jobs.rs, \
scraping/photo_import.rs, scraping/runner.rs.\n\
\n\
2. server/src/scraping/steps.rs (1148 lines) holds six pipeline steps \
(FetchHtmlStep, FetchImagesStep, SaveRecipeStep, ApplyNormalizedTitleStep, \
ApplyGeneratedDescriptionStep, ApplyAutoTagsStep) plus helpers in one file. \
Split into scraping/steps/ with one file per step and a shared helpers \
module.\n\
\n\
3. run_photo_import_job (mod.rs:465-566) has eleven near-identical error arms \
that log, call mark_failed, discard its Result with `let _ =`, and return — \
both duplicated and silently ignoring DB failures when marking a job failed \
(fail-fast violation). Extract a run_photo_import_job_inner(...) -> Result<(), \
ScrapeError> and call mark_failed once at the boundary, mirroring the \
run_scrape_job/run_scrape_job_inner split already at mod.rs:780/796.\n\
\n\
Mostly mechanical; no extraction/parsing behavior change, so no `make \
pipeline` data/ diffs expected.",
